// PARAM: --analysis interval
// Two call sites to the same procedure share ONE activation context
// (--graph-snapshot shows both "enter square(...)" edges landing on the
// same cluster_ctx_1): square's entry is one CFG node, revisited once per
// call site, not resolved per call site. This is call-site (in)sensitivity
// -- a context-sensitivity gap distinct from (and not fixed by) the
// Base-style D/G migration that resolved 04-globals/precision/
// 02-global_var.vimp's flow-insensitive global summary: even with the
// whole abstract state lifted into the local unknown, the entry node
// itself is still keyed on the unit context, so the D/G solver evaluates
// it once against both incoming edges. Under the warrowing update rule
// this repeated evaluation widens the entered parameter's bound on the
// second visit, so neither call's own exact argument (9 or 16) survives
// -- both checks come back UNKNOWN, not a narrower sound join. A
// call-string- or entry-state-context-sensitive analysis (see
// Interval_Ctx_Entry_State_Sound, out of scope here) would key the entry per
// call site instead.
int32 square(int32 n) {
  return n * n
}
void main() {
  int32 a, b;
  a := square(3);
  b := square(4);
  __voblint_check(a == 9); // UNKNOWN
  __voblint_check(b == 16) // UNKNOWN
}
